      {
        "id": 71272,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-29T00:06:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Amnachaidh\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ba8739/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Amnachaidh:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Back to topic, do other people use \"plink\" to refer to doing one target one point of damage?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I never heard \"plink\" before I came onto this forum, but now I'm inclined toward using it.&nbsp; Although I make a lot of other assorted sounds during actual RL play (not on every hit, but not restricted to just 1 damage hits either; it can befor anything that hits anything for any amount, depending on my mood) - \"SPANG!\" is my favorite, but \"dunc-!\" and \"bung!\" also appear now and again.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I use NOPE (TF2 Engineer voice) to refer to damage that is blocked completely, either by immunity, meat shields, standard DR, what have you.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That makes me think of <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0852.html\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">this</a>…</p>",
